I've made a few vlog type videos  recently and I really like the concept  of recording aspects of your life  regardless of whether people view it or  not I feel like recording your life  through the vlog form that's become more  popular it's something that I really  appreciate I often think it's kind of a  shame that we lose so much of our life  through not recording it to me the idea  of memory is such a huge component of  who we are one of my biggest fears is  losing my memories because I feel like  that is losing Who I am the memories  that I have define what I like and what  I do and I feel like they're the essence  of my personality I only remember a  fraction of the things that happened to  me  and I wonder does that make me only kind  of a fraction of Who I am is it really a  shame that I lose so much of my life I  actually kind of like the idea of  recording every part of your life and  sort of that sci-fi sense or following  being followed around with a 360 camera  and being able to log memories as they  really happened this concept was  explored in a recent episode of the show  black mirror and in the episode a guy  has through a implant in his eye the  ability to record everything that  happens and to sift through the memories  at first I'm like oh that's so awesome  what happens in this show without too  many spoilers is that he kind of goes  mad from the idea of having that ability  to relive everything whether it's a good  or a horrible experience I guess that's  the natural conclusion of the idea that  we wouldn't be able to handle recording  everything that there are things better  left forgotten that purging our minds is  the only way we can continue to live and  go forwards but I also think the episode  was a little bit unfair to the idea they  sort of jump straight to the conclusion  that this is going to be bad without  really showing how it can change the  fundamental way we live our lives I  don't deny that it would probably be a  bad idea to be able to remember  everything I'm certainly sure there are  things I'm glad I've forgotten but I  still like the idea or at least the idea  of recording a little bit more but is  this a totally mad idea I'm not sure  that let me know would you want to  record aspects of your life maybe even  not for your own use but just as sort of  a digital immortality
 

